#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows.rst:78
#: a3230acad2974b0abca37f628c0acb2a
msgid ""
"Windows ISOs can be downloaded directly from Microsoft (e.g., `here <https://"
"www.microsoft.com/en-us/software-download/windows10ISO>`__ for Win10), or "
"selected and downloaded via the `Windows Media Creation Tool <https://"
"go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?LinkId=691209>`__. You should, however, regard the "
"downloaded image to be untrustworthy, since there is no reliable way to "
"check that the download was not somehow compromised (see the discussion in "
"issue `Simplify Qubes Windows Tools Installation for R4.1 #7240 <https://"
"github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/issues/7240>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows.rst:80
#: 02ca2e74ab9241eaa2e3f23e0df2ccdf
msgid ""
"Unofficial “debloated” ISOs from projects like reviOS 18 or ameliorated 10 "
"can be found on the net, although obviously you should consider them even "
"“unsafer” than MS-provided ISOs. Alternatively, one could download an "
"official ISO and run scripts/apply patches before installation. Some of the "
"“tweaks” might end up being too much depending on the qube’s planned usage, "
"though (e.g., no appx functionality in ameliorated Windows - so the "
"installation of Windows Store apps is impossible, even with PowerShell)."
msgstr ""

